IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), Part IV: Increases for dependants, ss 80-93.
-- ss 80 to 86 and s 90 are shown blank in this text. LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Plain-text rendering by a converter script, not the official text.
-- BAR POLARITY: a "shall not be entitled" function answers "is the person barred?": JUST TRUE = the text says not entitled;
-- JUST FALSE = the text says no bar (a failed "if"); NOTHING = the rule is silent on the case.

§ `Part IV -- Increases for dependants`

§§ `s 86A -- Incapacity benefit: increase for adult dependants`

-- s 86A(1): the weekly rates of short-term and long-term incapacity benefit "shall, in such circumstances as may be prescribed, be increased for adult dependants by the appropriate amount specified ... in Schedule 4, Part IV, column (3)".
-- The prescribed circumstances are outside the sources and the Schedule 4 table is omitted from this text, so both are inputs. The result is the amount of the increase.
-- src:2229 | (1) The weekly rates of short-term and long-term incapacity benefit shall, in such circumstances as may be prescribed, be increased for adult dependants by the appropriate amount specified in relation to benefit of that description in Schedule 4, Part IV, column (3).
@ref s 86A(1) (src:2229)
GIVEN `the circumstances prescribed for an increase for an adult dependant are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 4 pt IV col 3 the appropriate amount for an adult dependant in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 86A(1) the increase of incapacity benefit for an adult dependant in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the circumstances prescribed for an increase for an adult dependant are met`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `sch 4 pt IV col 3 the appropriate amount for an adult dependant in pounds`    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) if the Schedule 4 figure is not supplied
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rates "shall, in such circumstances as may be prescribed, be increased"; the text does not say there is no increase otherwise
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the circumstances are prescribed by regulations that are not among the sources

-- s 86A(2): regulations may provide that no increase is given where the dependant's earnings exceed a prescribed amount (a regulation-making power; inert, machinery).

§§ `s 87 -- Rate of increase where associated retirement pension is attributable to reduced contributions`

-- s 87(1): where a person (a) is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under s 30A(2)(b) and (b) would have been entitled only by virtue of s 60(1) to the retirement pension by reference to which the rate is determined,
-- "the amount of any increase of the benefit attributable to sections 82 to 86A above shall be determined in accordance with regulations under this section". The answer for (b) is s 60's (seam S22, another part's range).
-- src:2232 | (1) Where a person—
-- src:2233 | (a) is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under section 30A(2)(b) above; and
-- src:2234 | (b) would have been entitled only by virtue of section 60(1) above to the retirement pension by reference to which the rate of that benefit ... is determined,
-- src:2235 | the amount of any increase of the benefit attributable to sections 82 to 86A above shall be determined in accordance with regulations under this section.
@ref s 87(1) (src:2232-2235)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under section 30A(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 60(1) the retirement pension would be payable only by virtue of section 60` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87(1) the amount of any increase is determined in accordance with regulations under this section` MEANS
    IF   `the person is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under section 30A(2)(b)` AND (`s 60(1) the retirement pension would be payable only by virtue of section 60` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for the case "Where a person" is within (a) and (b); the answer for (b) is section 60's and may not be supplied

-- s 87(2): "The regulations shall not provide for any such increase in a case where the retirement pension ... (a) would have been payable only by virtue of section 60; and (b) would, in consequence of a failure to satisfy a contribution condition, have contained no basic pension."
-- src:2236 | (2) The regulations shall not provide for any such increase in a case where the retirement pension by reference to which the rate of the said benefit ... is determined—
-- src:2237 | (a) would have been payable only by virtue of section 60 above; and
-- src:2238 | (b) would, in consequence of a failure to satisfy a contribution condition, have contained no basic pension.
@ref s 87(2) (src:2236-2238)
GIVEN `s 60(1) the retirement pension would be payable only by virtue of section 60` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the retirement pension would, in consequence of a failure to satisfy a contribution condition, have contained no basic pension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87(2) the person is barred from an increase under the regulations` MEANS
    IF   (`s 60(1) the retirement pension would be payable only by virtue of section 60` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the retirement pension would, in consequence of a failure to satisfy a contribution condition, have contained no basic pension`
    THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative): "The regulations shall not provide for any such increase in a case where"
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for "a case where" both (a) and (b) hold

§§ `s 88 -- Increases to be in respect of only one adult dependant`

-- s 88: "A person shall not by virtue of section 86A above be entitled for the same period to an increase of benefit in respect of more than one person."
-- src:2240 | A person shall not by virtue of section 86A above be entitled for the same period to an increase of benefit in respect of more than one person.
@ref s 88 (src:2240)
GIVEN `the number of persons in respect of whom the person claims an increase under section 86A for the same period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 88 the person is barred from an increase in respect of a further person for the same period` MEANS
    IF   `the number of persons in respect of whom the person claims an increase under section 86A for the same period` GREATER THAN 1
    THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative): "A person shall not by virtue of section 86A above be entitled for the same period to an increase of benefit in respect of more than one person"
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is for "more than one person"

§§ `s 89 -- Earnings to include occupational and personal pensions etc.`

-- s 89(3): "PPF periodic payments" MEANS (a) periodic compensation payments under the pension compensation provisions (s 162(2) Pensions Act 2004 or Art 146(2) of the 2005 Order); or (b) periodic payments under s 166 of the 2004 Act or Art 150 of the 2005 Order,
-- other than payments made to a surviving dependant of a person entitled to such compensation.
-- src:2246 | (3) In this section “PPF periodic payments” means—
-- src:2247 | (a) any periodic compensation payments made in relation to a person, payable under the pension compensation provisions as specified in section 162(2) of the Pensions Act 2004 or Article 146(2) of the Pensions (Northern Ireland) Order 2005 (the pension compensation provisions); or
-- src:2248 | (b) any periodic payments made in relation to a person, payable under section 166 of the Pensions Act 2004 or Article 150 of the Pensions (Northern Ireland) Order 2005 (duty to pay scheme benefits unpaid at assessment date etc.),
-- src:2249 | other than payments made to a surviving dependant of a person entitled to such compensation.
@ref s 89(3) (src:2246-2249)
GIVEN `the payment is a periodic compensation payment payable under the pension compensation provisions as specified in section 162(2) of the Pensions Act 2004 or Article 146(2) of the Pensions (Northern Ireland) Order 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is a periodic payment payable under section 166 of the Pensions Act 2004 or Article 150 of the Pensions (Northern Ireland) Order 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is made to a surviving dependant of a person entitled to such compensation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 89(3) the payment is a PPF periodic payment` MEANS
    IF   (`the payment is a periodic compensation payment payable under the pension compensation provisions as specified in section 162(2) of the Pensions Act 2004 or Article 146(2) of the Pensions (Northern Ireland) Order 2005`
          OR `the payment is a periodic payment payable under section 166 of the Pensions Act 2004 or Article 150 of the Pensions (Northern Ireland) Order 2005`)
         AND (NOT (`the payment is made to a surviving dependant of a person entitled to such compensation`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“PPF periodic payments” means ... other than payments made to a surviving dependant of a person entitled to such compensation"

-- s 89(1): "Except as may be prescribed, in ... sections 82 and 86A above, and in regulations under section 86A above, any reference to earnings includes a reference to payments by way of occupational or personal pension."
-- src:2243 | (1) Except as may be prescribed, in ... sections 82 and 86A above, and in regulations under section 86A above, any reference to earnings includes a reference to payments by way of occupational or personal pension.
@ref s 89(1) (src:2243)
GIVEN `the payment is by way of occupational or personal pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an exception is prescribed for the payment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 89(1) the payment counts as earnings in sections 82 and 86A` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the payment is by way of occupational or personal pension`) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "any reference to earnings includes" payments by way of pension; other payments are not decided by this sentence
        IF `an exception is prescribed for the payment` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as may be prescribed"
        IF `an exception is prescribed for the payment` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the exceptions are prescribed by regulations that are not among the sources

-- s 89(1A): the same for PPF periodic payments.
-- src:2244 | (1A) Except as may be prescribed, in sections 82 and 86A above, and in regulations under section 86A above, any reference to earnings includes a reference to payments by way of PPF periodic payments.
@ref s 89(1A) (src:2244)
GIVEN `the payment is a PPF periodic payment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an exception is prescribed for the payment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 89(1A) the PPF periodic payment counts as earnings in sections 82 and 86A` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the payment is a PPF periodic payment` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "any reference to earnings includes" PPF periodic payments; other payments are not decided by this sentence
        IF `an exception is prescribed for the payment` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as may be prescribed"
        IF `an exception is prescribed for the payment` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the exceptions are prescribed by regulations that are not among the sources

-- s 89(2): the Secretary of State may by regulations provide for apportionment of pension payments made otherwise than weekly (a regulation-making power; inert, machinery).

§§ `s 91 -- Effect of trade disputes on entitlement to increases`

-- s 91(2): "A person falls within this subsection if" (a) he is prevented from being entitled to a jobseeker's allowance by section 14 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (trade disputes); or (b) he would be so prevented if he were otherwise entitled to that benefit.
-- src:2257 | (2) A person falls within this subsection if—
-- src:2258 | (a) he is prevented from being entitled to a jobseeker’s allowance by section 14 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (trade disputes); or
-- src:2259 | (b) he would be so prevented if he were otherwise entitled to that benefit.
@ref s 91(2) (src:2257-2259)
GIVEN `he is prevented from being entitled to a jobseeker's allowance by section 14 of the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he would be so prevented if he were otherwise entitled to that benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(2) the person falls within this subsection` MEANS
    IF   `he is prevented from being entitled to a jobseeker's allowance by section 14 of the Jobseekers Act 1995` OR `he would be so prevented if he were otherwise entitled to that benefit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person falls within this subsection if"

-- s 91(1): "A beneficiary shall not be entitled (a) to an increase in any benefit under or by virtue of sections 82 to 88 above; or (b) to an increase in benefit ... by virtue of regulations under section 90 above, if the person in respect of whom he would be entitled to the increase falls within subsection (2) below."
-- src:2253 | (1) A beneficiary shall not be entitled—
-- src:2254 | (a) to an increase in any benefit under or by virtue of sections 82 to 88 above; or
-- src:2255 | (b) to an increase in benefit ... by virtue of regulations under section 90 above,
-- src:2256 | if the person in respect of whom he would be entitled to the increase falls within subsection (2) below.
@ref s 91(1) (src:2253-2256)
GIVEN `the person in respect of whom the beneficiary would be entitled to the increase falls within subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(1) the beneficiary is barred from the increase by a trade dispute` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person in respect of whom the beneficiary would be entitled to the increase falls within subsection (2)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative): "A beneficiary shall not be entitled ... if the person in respect of whom he would be entitled to the increase falls within subsection (2) below"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be entitled ... if the person ... falls within subsection (2)" does not apply to one who does not
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer for subsection (2) is not supplied

§§ `s 92 -- Dependency increases: continuation of awards in cases of fluctuating earnings`

-- s 92(1), first limb: where a beneficiary (a) has been awarded an increase under this Part, but (b) ceases to be entitled by reason only that the weekly earnings of another person ("the relevant earner") exceed the amount of the increase or a specified amount,
-- "then, if and so long as the beneficiary would have continued to be entitled to the increase, disregarding any such excess of earnings, the award shall continue in force".
-- src:2261 | (1) Where a beneficiary—
-- src:2262 | (a) has been awarded an increase of benefit under this Part of this Act, but
-- src:2263 | (b) ceases to be entitled to the increase by reason only that the weekly earnings of some other person (“the relevant earner”) exceed the amount of the increase or, as the case may be, some specified amount,
-- src:2264 | then, if and so long as the beneficiary would have continued to be entitled to the increase, disregarding any such excess of earnings, the award shall continue in force but the increase shall not be payable for any week if the earnings relevant to that week exceed the amount of the increase or, as the case may be, the specified amount.
@ref s 92(1) (src:2261-2264)
GIVEN `the beneficiary has been awarded an increase of benefit under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary ceases to be entitled to the increase by reason only that the weekly earnings of the relevant earner exceed the amount of the increase or a specified amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary would have continued to be entitled to the increase, disregarding any such excess of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92(1) the award continues in force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the beneficiary has been awarded an increase of benefit under this Part` AND `the beneficiary ceases to be entitled to the increase by reason only that the weekly earnings of the relevant earner exceed the amount of the increase or a specified amount`) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for "Where a beneficiary (a) has been awarded an increase ... but (b) ceases to be entitled to the increase by reason only that" the relevant earner's earnings exceed the amount
        IF `the beneficiary would have continued to be entitled to the increase, disregarding any such excess of earnings` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "then, if and so long as the beneficiary would have continued to be entitled to the increase, disregarding any such excess of earnings, the award shall continue in force"

-- s 92(1), second limb: "the increase shall not be payable for any week if the earnings relevant to that week exceed the amount of the increase or, as the case may be, the specified amount."
-- Earnings equal to the amount do not "exceed" it.
-- src:2264 | then, if and so long as the beneficiary would have continued to be entitled to the increase, disregarding any such excess of earnings, the award shall continue in force but the increase shall not be payable for any week if the earnings relevant to that week exceed the amount of the increase or, as the case may be, the specified amount.
@ref s 92(1) (src:2264)
GIVEN `the award continues in force` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the earnings relevant to the week in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the increase or the specified amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92(1) the increase is barred from payment for the week by the relevant earner's earnings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the award continues in force` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is part of the continuation rule
        IF `the earnings relevant to the week in pounds` GREATER THAN `the amount of the increase or the specified amount in pounds` THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative): "the increase shall not be payable for any week if the earnings relevant to that week exceed the amount of the increase"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be payable for any week if the earnings relevant to that week exceed" does not apply when they do not

-- s 92(2): "In this section the earnings which are relevant to any week are those earnings of the relevant earner which, apart from this section, would be taken into account in determining whether the beneficiary is entitled to the increase in question for that week."
-- src:2265 | (2) In this section the earnings which are relevant to any week are those earnings of the relevant earner which, apart from this section, would be taken into account in determining whether the beneficiary is entitled to the increase in question for that week.
@ref s 92(2) (src:2265)
GIVEN `the earnings of the relevant earner in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `apart from this section they would be taken into account in determining whether the beneficiary is entitled to the increase for that week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 92(2) the earnings relevant to the week in pounds` MEANS
    IF   `apart from this section they would be taken into account in determining whether the beneficiary is entitled to the increase for that week`
    THEN JUST `the earnings of the relevant earner in pounds`
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the earnings which are relevant to any week are those earnings ... which ... would be taken into account"; earnings not so taken into account are not stated to be irrelevant in so many words

§§ `s 93 -- Dependency increases on termination of employment after a period of entitlement to disability working allowance`

-- s 93(b): the regulations under which the benefit was last increased in respect of a dependant.
-- src:2271 | (b) when he was last entitled to that benefit ... , it was increased in respect of a dependant by virtue of—
-- src:2272 | (i) regulation 8(6) of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Regulations 1977;
-- src:2273 | (ii) regulation 2 of the Social Security (Savings for Existing Beneficiaries) Regulations 1984;
-- src:2274 | (iii) regulation 3 of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Amendment Regulations 1984; or
-- src:2275 | (iv) regulation 4 of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency and Computation of Earnings) Amendment Regulations 1989,
-- src:2276 | for the purpose of determining whether his benefit ... should be increased by virtue of that regulation for any period beginning with the day on which he again becomes entitled to his benefit ... , the increase in respect of that dependant shall be treated as having been payable to him on each day between the last day on which his benefit ... was previously payable and the day on which he again becomes entitled to it.
@ref s 93 (src:2271-2276)
DECLARE `s 93(b) Regulation` IS ONE OF
    `s 93(b)(i) regulation 8(6) of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Regulations 1977`
    `s 93(b)(ii) regulation 2 of the Social Security (Savings for Existing Beneficiaries) Regulations 1984`
    `s 93(b)(iii) regulation 3 of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Amendment Regulations 1984`
    `s 93(b)(iv) regulation 4 of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency and Computation of Earnings) Amendment Regulations 1989`
    `s 93(b) another provision`

-- s 93: "Where (a) a person becomes entitled (i) to the higher rate of short-term incapacity benefit, or to long-term incapacity benefit, by virtue of section 30C(5) or (6) or section 42 above ...; (b) when he was last entitled to that benefit ..., it was increased in respect of a dependant by virtue of" one of four regulations,
-- "for the purpose of determining whether his benefit ... should be increased by virtue of that regulation for any period beginning with the day on which he again becomes entitled to his benefit ..., the increase in respect of that dependant shall be treated as having been payable to him on each day between the last day on which his benefit was previously payable and the day on which he again becomes entitled to it."
-- "between": taken to exclude the two days named, since the benefit was payable on the first and he is entitled again on the second (fork F5 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2267 | Where—
-- src:2268 | (a) a person becomes entitled—
-- src:2269 | (i) to the higher rate of short-term incapacity benefit, or to long-term incapacity benefit, by virtue of section 30C(5) or (6) or section 42 above, ...
-- src:2270 | (ii) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:2271 | (b) when he was last entitled to that benefit ... , it was increased in respect of a dependant by virtue of—
-- src:2272 | (i) regulation 8(6) of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Regulations 1977;
-- src:2273 | (ii) regulation 2 of the Social Security (Savings for Existing Beneficiaries) Regulations 1984;
-- src:2274 | (iii) regulation 3 of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency) Amendment Regulations 1984; or
-- src:2275 | (iv) regulation 4 of the Social Security Benefit (Dependency and Computation of Earnings) Amendment Regulations 1989,
-- src:2276 | for the purpose of determining whether his benefit ... should be increased by virtue of that regulation for any period beginning with the day on which he again becomes entitled to his benefit ... , the increase in respect of that dependant shall be treated as having been payable to him on each day between the last day on which his benefit ... was previously payable and the day on which he again becomes entitled to it.
@ref s 93 (src:2267-2276)
GIVEN `s 30C(5) the person is entitled to the higher rate of short-term incapacity benefit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 42 the person is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the regulation by virtue of which the benefit was last increased in respect of the dependant` IS A `s 93(b) Regulation`
      `the last day on which his benefit was previously payable` IS A DATE
      `the day on which he again becomes entitled to his benefit` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93 the increase in respect of the dependant is treated as having been payable to the person on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT ((day GREATER THAN `the last day on which his benefit was previously payable`) AND (day LESS THAN `the day on which he again becomes entitled to his benefit`)) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on each day between the last day on which his benefit was previously payable and the day on which he again becomes entitled to it"
        IF `the regulation by virtue of which the benefit was last increased in respect of the dependant` EQUALS `s 93(b) another provision` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for an increase "by virtue of" one of the four regulations named
        IF (`s 30C(5) the person is entitled to the higher rate of short-term incapacity benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 42 the person is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answers for sections 30C and 42 are another part's and are not supplied; the Act does not say what follows if the person is not so entitled
